{
 "name": "\"An opponent has 10 or less life\" reads the opponents' life totals",
 "notes": "The generic 'has [ability]' condition branch read 'an opponent has 10 or less life' as an ability named '10 or less life', so the condition was never true. A life branch now reads any opponent (or a / each player) of the source's controller, and the 'X and Y' split recognises 'an opponent has', so Blood Baron of Vizkopa reads both halves. Life: Player 1 30, Player 2 8, Player 3 20; Player 2's tab is open. Player 1's Bloodghast has haste, Ruthless Cullblade 4/2, Blood Baron 10/10 with flying. Player 2's Guul Draz Vampire (opponents at 30 and 20) stays 1/1 without intimidate. Memory: project_opponent_life_conditions_2026-10-14.",
